# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the test suites, used as
#
#   TSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=test/tsan.supp" python3 test/run-spec-test.py ...
#
# What a guest program does to a shared linear memory is allowed to race: the threads proposal
# gives an unsynchronized access a defined outcome - one of the values written - and the spec's
# own tests (nested, MP, SB, LB, thread, ...) do it on purpose, to see that an engine copes.
# The interpreter performs those accesses as the plain loads, stores and bulk operations they
# are, which is what ThreadSanitizer reports, so they are named here and nothing else is:
# every atomic access, the waiter queue, the memory's length and the runtime's own state stay
# in view.

race:op_*_Load_*
race:op_*_Store_*
race:op_MemCopy*
race:op_MemFill*
race:op_MemInit*
